THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
================================================================

The Windows x64 default backend is the complete official Niubash v1.5.0
portable distribution, embedded unchanged under runtime/win32-x64/niubash.
Source: https://github.com/unixwin/niubash/releases/tag/v1.5.0
The archive and complete file inventory are SHA-256 pinned and verified
before staging or execution. bash-runtime install acquires this same
archive into an operator-managed DSH_HOME copy, not PortableGit.

Niubash and its rubash library and WinuxCmd are MIT-licensed. The complete
upstream package also carries gawk (GPL-3.0-or-later), niugit (GPL-2.0-only),
ripgrep (MIT OR Unlicense), fd (MIT OR Apache-2.0), and the DLL closure
listed in licenses/dll-closure. Their license texts, provenance and
corresponding-source pointers are retained in the payload's licenses/
directory. Upstream provenance is retained verbatim, including its version
labels; the frozen archive inventory is the authority for shipped bytes.
Per-call command faces are derived only from the verified WinuxCmd binary;
the immutable source distribution is not modified by shell execution.

PortableGit is no longer a default optional dependency. The explicit legacy
Git Bash build/provision path retains the pinned Git for Windows
v2.56.0.windows.2 (GPL-2.0) for compatibility. Upstream source and terms:
https://github.com/git-for-windows/git and https://github.com/git/git.
Existing operator-selected Git Bash installations are not removed.

  * PowerShell remains managed by the host. `dsh-ops upgrade-host-pwsh`
    previews a standard Windows installation and `--yes` executes WinGet.
    It does not override the host executor or remove existing copies.
    The legacy provisioner retains a PIN, not a redistribution.
    This distribution does not contain, forward, repackage, or
    redistribute PowerShell. The pin records the upstream release
    (`PowerShell-7.6.6-win-x64.zip`, PowerShell `v7.6.6`), the official
    URL that publishes it, and its SHA-256; `dsh-ops provision-shells
    --pwsh` reads the pin, downloads that asset on the user's own
    machine, and verifies the digest there; OPS does not automatically
    activate that legacy copy. PowerShell is distributed by
    Microsoft under the MIT licence; that licence text, its copyright,
    and the corresponding source belong to Microsoft and to the
    PowerShell project (https://github.com/PowerShell/PowerShell).

